{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"148f980f56c19d5d","type":"text","text":"==Death & curses==","x":-98,"y":-23,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f8c25c7cd6a4b7af","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Death is a common occurrence amongst exorcists, both for those that are victims of it, and for those deeply intimate with the grief that follows after. There is nothing in the known universe that can avoid this fate forever. Even those who hold the world on their shoulders, those who have defied heaven, and those whose cerulean tears fall over the earth will one day find themselves at the end of their story","x":340,"y":-104,"width":520,"height":223},
		{"id":"100633f0f9c463e6","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Every single person who has ever died has had their Last Words, prepared or otherwise: \n> \n> “Ay… tell my mama I loved her, ‘Kay?” \n> “I’ll be home soon.” \n> “Do as you must. Heaven’s Eye.” \n> “For hate’s sake, I spit my last breath at thee.” \n> \n> “...I’m sorry.”","x":1100,"y":-134,"width":520,"height":284},
		{"id":"051d10a929159a3c","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> For exorcists, those who have died with too many regrets, their ==Last Words== possess more power over the world than they think. In these fleeting moments, when an exorcist has died and ==chosen not to defy their fate==, they can use their last words to ==curse== a living being. Some attribute the effects of these curses to psychosomatic symptoms, while others believe them to be self-fulfilling prophecies on behalf of the cursed. TEMERITY denies the authenticity of these so-called curses, but a handful of exorcists know the weight these last words can bear.","x":1139,"y":360,"width":442,"height":378},
		{"id":"a9f149cdab7aebf6","type":"text","text":"*Narrative itself applies your will in the same breath it takes it, is not that incredible?*","x":1740,"y":511,"width":360,"height":76},
		{"id":"eae27c43b7bad4a5","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> In the moments before death, an exorcist must answer the following questions as truthfully as possible, and may expand upon their answers in any way of their choosing: \n> \n> - Can you blame someone for your death? \n>   \n> - Do you have any regrets? \n>   \n> - Can you describe a memory that flashes before your eyes?\n\n  \n  ","x":500,"y":398,"width":400,"height":302},
		{"id":"066bb1b1ec1b6f53","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> If the exorcist’s answers are sufficient, the admin may allow them to ==curse== someone in a way relating to one or more of their answers.","x":13,"y":680,"width":327,"height":195},
		{"id":"c54aabb7d129384f","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> A curse does not necessarily need to be negative or harmful as one might traditionally assume. What makes an exorcist's last words a curse is the fact that these words will continue to haunt another individual long after they are gone. They become words that never leave a person’s memories. They may latch onto the day-to-day moments of another’s life. They may even change someone’s fate.","x":-19,"y":980,"width":391,"height":321},
		{"id":"44234e0597790024","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Some examples of last words that can serve as curses are: \n> \n> “One day, you’ll find someone who will ==love you more than I ever could==.” \n> \n> “May every mirror ==show you exactly what you’ve become.==” \n> \n> ”I leave you to a ==lifetime of lukewarm coffees==.” \n> \n> “Do me a favour, will you? ==Die a miserable, lonely death==. It's the least you could do.” \n> \n> “==Don’t forget me==. No matter what\"","x":560,"y":946,"width":429,"height":390},
		{"id":"91111a0eee539c2d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> The admin treats these last words as a bargain of sorts, and fulfills them in a way of their choosing as the remaining exorcists’ story progresses. A curse could accomplish some nearly impossible things, such as an exorcist having faint memories of someone who has mass memory ruptured, or a sin’s lethal blow impossibly missing a vital organ. They could introduce a new NPC, or present themselves coming true naturally through the progression of the story. Or maybe they will simply serve as a small inconvenience for those who still remain.","x":1124,"y":977,"width":457,"height":328},
		{"id":"52ce1a93fc26e390","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> But for those who refuse to defy their own fate, perhaps they can defy the fate of others. ==So it goes==.","x":1660,"y":780,"width":330,"height":137},
		{"id":"421fbd7ea533cb7f","type":"text","text":"==Bound weapons==","x":-440,"y":-23,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1edaf9e609a2dd57","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> In 1679, a blacksmith off the coast of Anatolia injured himself while working a blade in his workshop, accidentally dripping his own blood onto the hot steel before quenching it. This weapon was being made for revenge, as a strange unknown beast had killed the smith’s late wife just the day before, and all weapons he had possessed turned brittle against the creature’s hide. He poured everything he had into this weapon, his soul, his body, and his grace. It was through fate alone that this individual was also psychically-sensitive, and unknowingly had performed the very first act of ==Grace-Binding==","x":-1020,"y":-205,"width":420,"height":424},
		{"id":"e8402f49003b6c74","type":"text","text":"*It was a gift of him and Him, both his soul and His eternity, of a romantic love and a passing one, of mortal and unreal, of tangible and what was not*\n\n*The piece remains by my side, of a sign of good will and prosperity, of something even further than temporary and never-lasting human connection*\n\n*It was a feeling, only presented to me, made a weapon, for my to use in his and His name until I can be free of my chains someday*\n\n*I miss you Andrew, I can only hope you to do, even if only reminiscing about the past*\n\n*And that I eventually moved on with my life, I am happy now* ","x":-1082,"y":-680,"width":544,"height":360},
		{"id":"3eed911e1262c807","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Grace-Binding is the act of transplanting a piece of one’s own psychic signature and seeding it within an object. This seed then continues to grow as the object is used, feeding off of the emotions and grace of its user, gaining new capabilities as an emerging supernatural being. Often causing long-term harm to the user, the act of Grace-Binding was removed from standard Exorcist options to maintain asset sustainability. But through TEMERITY experimentation, Grace-Binding’s application towards an exorcist’s weapons was deemed beneficial enough for the cost. Whether or not this program will remain in effect for the future of CAIN is yet to be seen.","x":-1680,"y":-205,"width":441,"height":424},
		{"id":"438baa444dff80c0","type":"text","text":"*Every tool, every weapon, every symbol, everything is a gift, passing done from person to person, from lovers, from friends, from families, from generations or nations*\n\n*They are unique and awake and eating your structure in the same way that worms do, but is more delicate, more personal, is not a beast feasting on your carcass or organs to keep itself alive*\n\n*Is a friend, another beating hearth, a soulmate, something that wants to keep you close and alive to not only allow you to live through hardship and strife*\n\n*It wants to change alongside your life, but only if you are ready to take this responsibility on your shoulders, as any kind of relationship between you beings need a two-road cooperation to persist*\n\n*It will surely outlast you, remember your mannerism and interest and name and achievements and be marked by your experiences and change forever...*","x":-1783,"y":-725,"width":544,"height":450},
		{"id":"e86d372b63da8d97","type":"text","text":"==CREATING A BOUND WEAPON==","x":-2260,"y":-18,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"b7f53a2d9777de94","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> A CAT 2 or higher exorcist may sign a contract to undergo the BOUND WEAPON experiment with TEMERITY. Upon creation of a bound weapon, an exorcist selects a single melee or ranged weapon that is separate from their service weapons, and infuses with their psychic energy through the following: \n> \n> - Select a type of Sin (Ogre, Hound, Lord, etc.) \n>   \n> - Answer a single trauma question for that sin classification as truthfully as possible. This answer is kept secret from the other exorcists. \n>   \n> - Select a single option from the enhancement board. The rules for selecting enhancements are located on the next page. \n>   \n> This weapon is bound to your soul, and contains a piece of the trauma that has made your exorcist who they are.","x":-2920,"y":-255,"width":440,"height":525},
		{"id":"2406a0a0134e9bd2","type":"text","text":"*...and one day, once you are gone too, millennial after you die*\n\n*It will still remember who you were in truth*\n\n","x":-2260,"y":-565,"width":287,"height":131},
		{"id":"4ad873460b74b112","type":"text","text":"*To form such a pact, is to make a call of trust between two individuals* \n\n*This promise, truth shared from flesh to non-existent, from an idea to something that just exists by itself without a cause*\n\n*Once this act of pure trust or convenience is made manifest*\n\n*It can't never be undone, except by death alone*","x":-2920,"y":-654,"width":452,"height":309},
		{"id":"be005f7badc369af","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==BINDING RITUAL==: In order to finalize the creation of your Bound Weapon, the player must write down their answer for the selected trauma question on a small piece of paper in real life. No one else must see what is written on that paper. Then the player must burn it, drown it, shred it, eat it, or destroy it in any means of their choice. When this piece of your exorcist has been cleansed from the world and kept in the deepest parts of you, ==the pact is sealed.==","x":-3480,"y":-192,"width":348,"height":399},
		{"id":"8a39069044196bd6","type":"text","text":"==USING A BOUND WEAPON==","x":-2825,"y":440,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c4cad9ba022da230","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Because a bound weapon is grown from their specific user’s trauma, they can only be effectively wielded by the person who has bound it, otherwise lashing out or acting uncontrollably in the hands of another. This bound weapon becomes a separate item from your traditional service weapon pair, and requires its own KP to retrieve during a mission. Upon drawing your bound weapon for the first time in a mission, sin surges through your body, testing your ability to control it. If you would suffer sin overflow and imago due to this, the bound weapon inevitably becomes a part of your new form, a dangerous liability for any exorcist squad.","x":-2300,"y":290,"width":480,"height":360},
		{"id":"df3b79794b34d1f9","x":-2245,"y":760,"width":371,"height":200,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> (Addendum: This is actually still considered your manifested coded weapon, following previously presented rules related to it, just changing when directly being referenced that)"},
		{"id":"68204e59a37da685","x":-1620,"y":339,"width":425,"height":263,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Whenever you survive a mission in which you successfully used your bound weapon at least once, you may spend an ==advance== to select a remaining trauma question from your original selected sin and answer it: then, select an additional option on the ==Enhancement Board==, and repeat the destruction ritual to finalize your upgrade."},
		{"id":"555c7b7e935c02eb","x":-1020,"y":352,"width":532,"height":238,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When selecting an enhancement for your Bound Weapon, you may select one of the options on these 2 pages or the next. For every enhancement a Bound Weapon has, its ==CAT== increases by ==+1==, to a ==maximum base CAT of 3==. As the number of trauma questions does not exceed 3, traditionally the maximum number of enhancements you can have on any single bound weapon is up to 3."},
		{"id":"e2ec6378be4eba26","x":-943,"y":723,"width":379,"height":417,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> All enhancements have a name, ==rating(R)==, and description. A Bound Weapon with no enhancements has a rating of 1, and enhancements added to it increase its rating by the indicated amount. Some enhancements are ==evolved==, and require your bound weapon to have the previous corresponding enhancement before being able to take it. The effects of an enhancement are only active while your bound weapon is retrieved from your kit and wielded by it’s owner (you), and remain inert while within your kit or not being wielded by you."},
		{"id":"4c3dfbc6059d3332","x":-932,"y":1300,"width":358,"height":363,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Many of the abilities and attributes of these upgrades may either affect the parameter of rolls such as difficulty or risk (even if not explicitly saying so), or gain or grant +1D to a specific action. The admin has discretion on when these effects take place or if effects would relevantly change the parameters of the narrative. Any bonus die granted through an enhanced weapon cannot exceed the +3D bonus die cap unless stated otherwise."},
		{"id":"2473fca9bfae0ad4","x":-1554,"y":723,"width":294,"height":148,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Enhancements board options are present in page 42-43-"},
		{"id":"9e4402cdc1f89c26","x":-306,"y":205,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==Inert=="},
		{"id":"4796c2373311ddbe","x":27,"y":139,"width":323,"height":193,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> - Coded passives are off\n> \n> - Sin is not being burned by round\n> \n> - works as described\n"},
		{"id":"fcec7cc5928c7e57","x":-340,"y":403,"width":321,"height":136,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Essentially, once the pact is done the stabilized manifestation works in two ways: Inert and active "},
		{"id":"372ba14618e7acfc","x":-332,"y":670,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==Active=="},
		{"id":"a6f8f6f40c4a655e","x":-387,"y":840,"width":305,"height":347,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> - Coded passives are on\n> - Suffer 1 sin loss after each round *after* the first active round pass\n> - Include all extra enhancements *available* after the extra CAT available with the passive related to the manifested weapon/tool "},
		{"id":"73162fb1a4ea93da","x":-878,"y":1842,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==GESTATION=="},
		{"id":"6629dbbebe0983cc","x":-932,"y":2060,"width":357,"height":460,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When you suffer a sin overflow that almost pushes you over the edge, your Bound Weapon may respond through gestation, a state in between that of an object and a minor sin itself. You may select one of the following enhancements for free after successfully resisting sin overflow with a modifier of +2 or higher on the final result. This enhancement does not count towards your bound weapon’s max enhancement capacity of 3. However once this option is taken, your Bound Weapon cannot gain any further enhancements, and has reached its final state."},
		{"id":"0c500a0006c07975","x":-880,"y":2720,"width":253,"height":75,"type":"text","text":"==Options for this event are present in pages 43-44=="},
		{"id":"d03426f1848fd7cf","x":-269,"y":-164,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==Expanded sins=="},
		{"id":"794908881e85bc15","x":-305,"y":-540,"width":322,"height":274,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Sins== are the stains of humanity to which exorcists have a duty to wipe off the face of the earth. Over the years they have been successful in this role, but the steady and inevitable rise of sin manifestation rates have given birth to ==new threats==."},
		{"id":"2f6f6f0c355ed501","x":189,"y":-595,"width":511,"height":385,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Sins are beginning to change in a way that is unexpected. Their durability, manifestation, and volatility have begun to fluctuate and differ vastly between subjects, and the Harpocrates Dossier has logged these ==advanced behaviors== and instances that CAIN has tried to ignore. Additionally, two new manifestation types have arisen in the past years, their true identity lost to misclassification and the hasty assumption that only the 6 primary sins were possible manifestations in sin hosts. The ==Spider== is a sin born from powerlessness and the desire to take control over everything around them. The ==Butcher== is a sin born from agony, whether physical or mental, and desires to inflict nothing but pain on everything around them."},
		{"id":"8ccc7ce736415774","x":202,"y":-1140,"width":485,"height":360,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Handlers are advised to exercise extreme caution when sending exorcist squads to execute these threats due to their unprecedented potential and new challenges they pose to exorcists beyond traditional hunts. Exorcists are also to be warned that ==alternate or additional traces== have been identified for the colloquially known 6 “core” sins, and may appear in the field. Catalogue the data that your team finds in the field to report back to ==TEMERITY==. Each day a new enemy arises. One day, one may arise that we ==cannot== defeat. Do what your kind does best. No matter how many times they show up, kill them again, and again, and **again**."},
		{"id":"4e46647388d61887","x":320,"y":-1401,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==Advanced behaviours== "}
	],
